---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Badge from "../../components/ui/Badge.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../lib/seo";
import "../../styles/prose.css";

const effectiveDate = "August 30, 2026";
const lastUpdated = "August 30, 2026";
const email = SITE.email;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="WhatsApp Business Platform Privacy Policy | SpaceDev"
  description="How SpaceDev handles data in connection with its WhatsApp Business Platform integration service. We do not receive, store, or process the content of WhatsApp messages."
  noindex={true}
  breadcrumbs={false}
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden" style="background: var(--sd-gradient-hero);">
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-6 md:px-10 pt-36 pb-20 md:pt-40 md:pb-28">
      <Badge tone="purple" class="mb-6">Legal</Badge>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl text-white">WhatsApp Business Platform Privacy Policy</h1>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-1 text-sm text-sd-text-muted">
        <p>Effective date: <time datetime="2026-08-30">{effectiveDate}</time></p>
        <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-08-30">{lastUpdated}</time></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <article class="sd-prose">
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This policy describes how SpaceDev S.A. ("SpaceDev", "we", "us"), a company registered in Uruguay
          with registered office at Bulevar España 2253, Piso 9, Montevideo, Uruguay, handles data in
          connection with our WhatsApp Business Platform integration service (the "Service").
        </p>
        <p>
          We are a Meta Tech Provider. The Service allows a business to connect a phone number it already uses
          in the WhatsApp Business App to the WhatsApp Cloud API, including in Coexistence mode, where the app
          on the phone and the API operate in parallel on the same number.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contact for privacy matters: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
        </p>

        <h2>2. Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This policy covers the Service only. It does not cover spacedev.io generally, our consulting
          engagements, or any other SpaceDev product.
        </p>
        <p>Two categories of people are relevant:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Customers</strong> — businesses that use the Service to connect a WhatsApp number, and developers or agencies acting on their behalf.</li>
          <li><strong>End users</strong> — people who exchange WhatsApp messages with a Customer's business number.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We have no direct relationship with End users. Our handling of data relating to End users is
          described in section 4.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Data we collect from Customers</h2>
        <div class="sd-table-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Source</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Business name, contact name, email, country</td><td>account administration, service notices</td><td>provided by the Customer</td></tr>
              <tr><td>WhatsApp Business Account ID (WABA ID), Meta Business Portfolio ID</td><td>provisioning and management of the connection</td><td>Meta, during Embedded Signup</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Business phone number ID, display phone number, verified name</td><td>phone number registration and identification of the connection</td><td>Meta</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Webhook endpoint URL and verification token</td><td>configuring webhook routing to the Customer's own server</td><td>provided by the Customer</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Access tokens issued by Meta</td><td>completing provisioning; see section 5</td><td>Meta</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Connection status, routing state, timestamps, error codes</td><td>operating the Service and diagnosing failures</td><td>generated by the Service</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Template status, template quality, account alerts, account review outcomes, business capability changes</td><td>notifying the Customer of events affecting their account</td><td>Meta webhooks</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>4. Message content — what we do not process</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not receive, inspect, store, forward, or replay the content of WhatsApp messages
          exchanged between a Customer's business and its End users.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>This is a property of how the Service is built, not only a commitment.</p>
        <p>
          During provisioning we configure a WABA-level webhook override with Meta. Once that override is
          active, Meta delivers message-path webhook fields — including <code>messages</code>,
          <code>message_echoes</code>, <code>smb_message_echoes</code>, <code>smb_app_state_sync</code> and
          <code>history</code> — directly from Meta's servers to the endpoint the Customer controls. Those
          payloads do not transit our infrastructure.
        </p>
        <p>
          Webhook fields that Meta does not permit to be overridden — template status and quality updates,
          account updates, account alerts, account review outcomes, business capability updates and security
          events — are delivered to our application callback. These carry account and template metadata. They
          do not carry message content.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a message-path webhook reaches our callback because the override is not active or has failed, our
          system acknowledges the request without parsing, logging or storing its body, records that a routing
          failure occurred, and notifies the Customer that the connection is misconfigured.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>We maintain no database table for message content, in any form, including transient,
          diagnostic or debug storage.</strong>
        </p>

        <h3>What we can and cannot do</h3>
        <p>We want to be precise rather than reassuring.</p>
        <p>
          Because we are the Tech Provider, our Meta application holds permissions over the Customer's WhatsApp
          Business Account. That means we are technically able to issue new access tokens and to call Meta's API
          for that account. This is inherent to the Meta Tech Provider model and is true of every provider
          operating under it.
        </p>
        <p>
          What we commit to is narrower and verifiable: message traffic is not routed through our systems, we
          do not store message content, and any token issuance is recorded in an audit log available to the
          Customer.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Access tokens</h2>
        <p>
          By default, the Service operates in <strong>handoff mode</strong>: the access token obtained during
          Embedded Signup is delivered to the Customer and is not retained by us. We keep a one-way hash of the
          token solely to detect rotation, together with the WABA and business identifiers needed to administer
          the connection.
        </p>
        <p>
          A Customer may opt in to <strong>custody mode</strong>, in which we store the token encrypted at rest
          using AES-256-GCM with keys held outside the database. Opting in is explicit, is recorded in our audit
          log, and is displayed persistently in the Customer's dashboard. Custody mode is not enabled by default
          and is never enabled without the Customer's action.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Legal basis</h2>
        <p>Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies, we rely on:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Performance of a contract</strong> — providing the Service to the Customer.</li>
          <li><strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — securing the Service, preventing abuse, and diagnosing failures.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — where we must retain records by law.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Where Uruguayan Law No. 18.331 on the Protection of Personal Data applies, we process personal data
          on the basis of the Customer's consent and the performance of the contract, and we act as a data
          processor with respect to any personal data of End users that reaches us.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Roles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The <strong>Customer's business</strong> is the controller of personal data relating to its End users.</li>
          <li>Where a developer or agency operates the connection on behalf of a business, that party acts as a processor for that business.</li>
          <li><strong>SpaceDev</strong> provides provisioning infrastructure. With the webhook override active, we do not process End user message content. For the account and template metadata described in section 3, we act as a processor for the Customer.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          A data processing agreement is available to Customers on request and is required before custody mode
          is enabled.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Sharing</h2>
        <p>We share data with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Meta Platforms, Inc.</strong> — necessarily, to provision and manage the connection. Meta's handling of WhatsApp Business Platform data is governed by Meta's own terms and policies.</li>
          <li><strong>Infrastructure subprocessors</strong> — hosting, database and payment providers. A current list is available to Customers on request at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell data. We do not share data with advertisers. We do not use Customer data or account
          metadata to train machine learning models.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Retention</h2>
        <div class="sd-table-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Data</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Account and connection records</td><td>for the life of the account, then 90 days</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Management webhook events</td><td>90 days, then deleted automatically</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Audit log</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Failed onboarding sessions</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Message content</td><td>not applicable — never stored</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          Deletion is automated. A Customer may request earlier deletion of their account data at
          <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Security</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Encryption in transit (TLS 1.2 or higher) and at rest.</li>
          <li>Meta webhook signatures verified before any payload is processed.</li>
          <li>API credentials stored as one-way hashes.</li>
          <li>Webhook verification tokens and, where applicable, access tokens encrypted at rest.</li>
          <li>Access to production systems limited to named personnel and logged.</li>
          <li>Logging configured to exclude webhook request bodies.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          No system is perfectly secure. We will notify affected Customers without undue delay if a breach
          affecting their data occurs, and will comply with applicable notification requirements.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Data location and transfers</h2>
        <p>
          Our infrastructure is hosted in the United States (US East). Meta processes WhatsApp Business Platform
          data according to its own infrastructure and terms. Where personal data is transferred out of the
          European Economic Area, we rely on Standard Contractual Clauses.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you are, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to
          the processing of your personal data, to portability, and to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
          authority. In Uruguay, the supervisory authority is the Unidad Reguladora y de Control de Datos
          Personales (URCDP).
        </p>
        <p>
          Requests go to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We respond within 30 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because we do not hold End user message content, requests concerning WhatsApp message data should be
          directed to the business the End user was messaging.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Children</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone under
          16.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Compliance with Meta terms</h2>
        <p>
          Our use of data obtained through the WhatsApp Business Platform complies with the Meta Platform Terms,
          the WhatsApp Business Terms of Service, and Meta's Developer Policies. We use that data only to provide
          the Service to the Customer whose account it relates to.
        </p>

        <h2>15. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We will post material changes on this page and update the date above. Where required, we will notify
          Customers directly.
        </p>

        <h2>16. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          SpaceDev S.A.<br />
          Bulevar España 2253, Piso 9, Montevideo, Uruguay<br />
          <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
